. The race has drawn top-tier attention: Trump has campaigned in San Antonio, and House Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries has appeared for Garcia.\n\nSix of ten expert ratings call the district Lean Republican, three call it a Tossup, and one leans Democratic. The only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from late August, showed De La Cruz ahead by a point, while prediction markets price Garcia near 61 percent to win. A national climate favoring Democrats this cycle appears to offset much of the district's Republican lean, leaving the contest effectively even, with sparse and dated polling keeping uncertainty wide.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4325, "margin": -0.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5895, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6117, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6193, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5254, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5283, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5907, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6027, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6095, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5948, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.596, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5662, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.594, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.527, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.539, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3993, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3992, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4712, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.5262, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.5023, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.5645, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.4968, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.5435, "margin": 0.7}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.5285, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "20